applicable across jurisdictions.\n\nWrite in flowing paragraphs.\n\n### SLOT 3: Quantitative Acceptance Criteria versus Project-Specific Assessment\n\nThe surveyed sources are examined with respect to whether they supply quantitative acceptance criteria for blasting effects on TSFs, or whether they require project-specific assessment, monitoring, laboratory characterization, and engineering judgement in lieu of fixed thresholds.\n\nWrite in flowing paragraphs.\n\n### SLOT 4: Report Framing to Distinguish Criteria, Monitoring Requirements, and Assumptions\n\nThe appropriate framing in a technical report that distinguishes published reference criteria, project-specific criteria, monitoring requirements, and analysis assumptions - such that no generic building-vibration criterion is implied as governing TSF safety - is addressed.\n\nWrite in flowing paragraphs.\n\n### SLOT 5: Source-Backed Terminology for TSF Response to Blasting\n\nSource-backed terminology drawn from the relevant guidance literature for describing TSF response to blasting is documented. The terms to be assessed include dynamic loading, transient vibration, pore-pressure generation, cyclic mobility, liquefaction potential, deformation, stability, monitoring, and related expressions as used in the authoritative sources.\n\nWrite in flowing paragraphs.\n\n## CONSTRAINTS\n\n- The output is in English.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
